    "title": "Report crash/recover crossing density as a first-class metric before steering on it",
    "description": "Pure-measurement change, no scheduler policy change. In spur-core/src/simulator/util_stats.rs add counters: crashes, recovers, messages dropped at crash, messages delivered to a node after a Recover that were dispatched before its Crash, and count of runs containing >=1 such crossing delivery. Plumb them through the explorer's per-batch stats output (spur-core/src/simulator/explorer.rs) so they appear alongside depthAtLeast/h2 in eval metrics. Gate emission behind an existing stats/verbosity flag rather than a new general config param so generalConfigParams does not grow. Run on the unmodified baseline scheduler to get the true crossing rate, then re-run with the crash-recover-density-knob patch applied locally to measure whether the bias raised it at all.",
